<title>VIETNAM: Vietnam's ailing president flown out of country.</title>
<headline>Vietnam's ailing president flown out of country.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam's President Le Duc Anh has been removed from the Hanoi 108 Army Hospital, where he had been in a critical condition, and flown out of the country, political sources said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>One of the sources said the 75-year-old general, one of the communist country's leadership troika, had been flown to Singapore on Tuesday and admitted to a hospital there.</p>
